      "id": "post_a7b4b30f",
      "slug": "welcome-to-the-blog",
      "title": "Welcome to the blog",
      "excerpt": "A quick hello and what to expect from My Blog.",
      "content": "## Hello there\n\nThis is your first post. You can edit it, delete it, or ask the AI assistant to rewrite it.\n\nHere's what you can do next:\n\n- **Pick a template** in the Design tab\n- **Write a post** in the Posts tab (or let AI draft one)\n- **Publish** to GitHub Pages in one click\n\n> Tip: everything you change is previewed live.",
      "tags": [
        "welcome"
      ],
      "date": "2026-09-03T09:25:04.430Z",
      "draft": false,
      "featured": true
    },
    {
      "id": "post_310153cb",
      "slug": "three-things-i-learned-this-week",
      "title": "Three things I learned this week",
      "excerpt": "Small lessons, big impact.",
      "content": "Every week I try to write down a few things I learned. Here are this week's.\n\n### 1. Start before you're ready\n\nWaiting for the perfect moment is a great way to never start.\n\n### 2. Keep it simple\n\nThe simplest version of an idea is usually the one people remember.\n\n### 3. Share it\n\nWriting in public is the fastest way to learn.",
      "tags": [
        "notes",
        "learning"
      ],
      "date": "2026-08-31T09:25:04.430Z",
      "draft": false,
      "featured": false
    },
    {
      "id": "post_ddef1f32",
      "slug": "how-this-site-was-made",
      "title": "How this site was made",
      "excerpt": "Built with a no-code AI blog builder and published to GitHub Pages.",
      "content": "This site was created with **Blog Builder** — no code required.\n\n1. Described the blog in a sentence\n2. Chose a template and a color style\n3. Hit publish\n\nThe whole thing is static HTML, so it loads fast and costs nothing to host.",
      "tags": [
